WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:01.533
Recall.

2
00:00:01.833 --> 00:00:03.223
The metric of miss cost.

3
00:00:03.223 --> 00:00:06.233
When a missed case is the disaster, this is the one.

4
00:00:07.433 --> 00:00:09.233
Recall is the mirror question.

5
00:00:09.533 --> 00:00:13.167
Of everything actually positive, how much did the model catch?

6
00:00:13.467 --> 00:00:15.717
Use it when a miss is the disaster.

7
00:00:15.717 --> 00:00:20.667
A screening test would rather raise ten false alarms than miss one real case.

8
00:00:21.867 --> 00:00:23.433
Use the same spam filter.

9
00:00:23.733 --> 00:00:26.283
Now look only at the actual spam row.

10
00:00:26.283 --> 00:00:29.867
Forty caught, ten missed, so fifty real spam emails.

11
00:00:30.167 --> 00:00:31.567
Forty of fifty caught.

12
00:00:31.567 --> 00:00:32.967
Recall is point eight.

13
00:00:34.167 --> 00:00:38.467
The formula: true positives over true positives plus false negatives.

14
00:00:38.767 --> 00:00:41.133
True positives are the cases we caught.

15
00:00:41.433 --> 00:00:44.433
False negatives are the ones that walked out the door.

16
00:00:45.633 --> 00:00:49.033
Precision and recall trade off through the decision threshold.

17
00:00:49.333 --> 00:00:51.713
Lower the threshold, and you flag more.

18
00:00:51.713 --> 00:00:52.567
Recall climbs.

19
00:00:52.867 --> 00:00:54.024
But precision falls.

20
00:00:54.024 --> 00:00:58.133
Which side to favor is a product decision about which error hurts more.

21
00:00:59.333 --> 00:01:02.300
In code, compute it by hand: forty over fifty.

22
00:01:02.600 --> 00:01:06.300
Then we take the predicted probabilities and try three thresholds.

23
00:01:06.600 --> 00:01:09.067
As the threshold drops, recall rises.

24
00:01:10.267 --> 00:01:12.033
Here is a two stage pipeline.

25
00:01:12.333 --> 00:01:19.700
First, a cheap screen over two hundred thousand candidates, tuned for recall point nine nine at a threshold of point two.

26
00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:25.467
A missed Earth twin is gone forever, while false alarms only cost the next stage some compute.

27
00:01:25.767 --> 00:01:30.200
Same model family, opposite threshold, because the cost of a miss differs.

28
00:01:31.400 --> 00:01:32.257
Let's recap.

29
00:01:32.257 --> 00:01:35.900
Recall is true positives over all actual positives.

30
00:01:36.200 --> 00:01:37.867
It is the metric of miss cost.

31
00:01:38.167 --> 00:01:41.767
Lower the threshold, and recall rises while precision falls.

32
00:01:42.067 --> 00:01:43.867
Next up: the F1 score.
